    "sections": [],
    "faqs": [
      {
        "question": "How do I check a accounting business name is free?",
        "answer": "Press Check on any name to see whether it's free as a company, a domain and a social media handle. In the UK, search Companies House; in the US, search your state's business register and the USPTO trade mark search. Check your local area too, as two similar names nearby confuse customers."
      },
      {
        "question": "What should I name my accounting firm?",
        "answer": "Clients want to trust you, so most firms use surnames (\"Hartley & Rowe Accountants\") or the town they serve; bookkeepers and tax preparers can be friendlier (\"Good Books Bookkeeping\"). Only use protected titles you hold: \"CPA\" in the US and \"Chartered\" in the UK need the right qualification, and Companies House asks for proof before it accepts \"Chartered\"."
      }
    ]
